Sora, Orbitron and Space Mono, latin subsets as served by Google Fonts

Vendored rather than fetched at runtime, so that what ships is what was reviewed
and the wallet never reaches out for a typeface. All three families are licensed
under the SIL Open Font License 1.1; each family's notice sits next to its file.

  sora-latin.woff2              Sora, variable weight 400 to 800, 25284 bytes
    source   https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/sora/v17/xMQ9uFFYT72X5wkB_18qmnndmSdSnh2BAfO5mnuyOo1lfiQwV6-x.woff2
    sha256   811e11966d29f3a01fcb19b087b61ac067d380665a55aebb7fcdf2cda95e4a93
    licence  sora.OFL.txt

  orbitron-700-latin.woff2      Orbitron, weight 700, 6528 bytes
    source   https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/orbitron/v35/yMJMMIlzdpvBhQQL_SC3X9yhF25-T1ny_CmBoWgz.woff2
    sha256   ee6acc5ad5349018f9ca71fab8118144160e110838931874150a1ac3f97db38d
    licence  orbitron.OFL.txt

  space-mono-400-latin.woff2    Space Mono, weight 400, 16520 bytes
    source   https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/spacemono/v17/i7dPIFZifjKcF5UAWdDRYEF8RQ.woff2
    sha256   fb4a81a2d0a893e5c38c394a7e716a1cef0b24610a0af49c96f6d529bd66bf2b
    licence  space-mono.OFL.txt

The files were resolved through
  https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Sora:wght@400;600&family=Orbitron:wght@700&family=Space+Mono&display=swap
requested with a Chrome user agent, taking the latin block of each face. The
notices come from https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl.

Verify a replacement before committing it:
  sha256sum *.woff2
